{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat control-reader-brief.md controls/control-packet-5.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage B: reading the control theses (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief\nand the one packet you are given.\n\nEach item of your packet pairs a **ruler question** (a question written by hand for an earlier, frozen measurement, with its\nunit, due day and ladder of rungs) with a **judged question** the system wrote itself for a thesis it opened (its question, the\noutcome it looks at, due day, year and rungs). It also lists **reader B's decisive items**: the evidence an earlier reader, called\nreader B, cited for the frozen answer to the ruler question (each with its day, title, passage and meaning), and **the evidence\nshown to the judge**: every evidence entry the system's judge was shown for the judged question in any of its requests on or\nbefore 2026-07-14 (empty when there is none). You are not told either answer, and you do not judge which answer is right.\n\nFor each item, answer three questions.\n\n1. `same_question`: **yes** when the judged question asks what the ruler question asks: the same quantity measured the same way\n   (the same total, scope and unit: not a part of it, a ceiling on it, another quantity or another unit), or the same event,\n   for the same period. **no** otherwise. Wording may differ; a judged question that asks for more or less than the ruler's,\n   or for another period, is **no**.\n2. `same_due`: for an **event** (a yes-or-no question), **yes** only when the judged question's deadline is the ruler's\n   deadline. For a **figure**, **yes** when the two due days both mark the publication of the same period's figure (for\n   example, both the annual report of the same fiscal year, even if the two days differ); **no** otherwise.\n3. `items`: for **each** of reader B's decisive items, by its id, **shown** when its content is present in the evidence shown to\n   the judge (the same fact or figure, in any wording, from any source), **not_shown** when it is absent. Search the entries for\n   the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a related item is.\n\nReturn one JSON object per item, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"control\": 3, \"same_question\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"same_due\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"items\": {\"i005\": \"shown\"|\"not_shown\", ...}, \"why\": \"one sentence naming what decides each no and each not_shown\"}`.\n\n## Third reader (only where the two readers differ)\n\nA third reader of each family is given this brief, the packet, and a list of the disputed points, each a control number and a\nfield (`same_question`, `same_due`, or `item <id>`), without the two readers' answers. For each point, answer that one question\nafresh by the rules above and return one JSON object per point, one per line, and nothing else:\n`{\"control\": 3, \"field\": \"item i005\", \"ruling\": \"yes\"|\"no\"|\"shown\"|\"not_shown\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}` (`yes`/`no` for the two\nquestion fields, `shown`/`not_shown` for an item).\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 10,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v4\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 450000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $392 billion and below $450 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 392000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 450000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $392 billion, below the cited analyst estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 392000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i281\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek Just Dealt Nvidia Stock a Potentially Major Blow\",\n    \"passage\": \"forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Q2 FY2027 revenue and gross-margin guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$91 billion ±2%; non-GAAP gross margin about 75%\",\n     \"period\": \"Q2 FY2027\",\n     \"condition\": \"assumes no China Data Center compute revenue\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i106\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA data-center compute revenue versus Wall Street consensus\",\n     \"how_much\": \"20% above consensus\",\n     \"period\": \"second half of fiscal 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027 and $554 billion in FY2028, versus trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\",\n   \"- e29 [fact; storagereview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:8c9d215416b714064de3b095 2026-07-03] NVIDIA made Omniverse freely available for development and production use as of May 2026, removing the production subscription requirement.\\n    Quote: As of May 2026, Omniverse is freely available for both development and production use,\",\n   \"- e30 [fact; Ben Wodecki, SDxCentral; original source Ashkan Seyedi ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] Ashkan Seyedi, formerly Nvidia’s lead for technical product marketing on co-packaged and pluggable interconnects, said he is taking the VP and GM role for AMS-Osram’s optical interconnect business line.\\n    Quote: Ashkan Seyedi had served as Nvidia’s lead for technical product marketing on its co-packaged and pluggable interconnect solutions since 2021. In a LinkedIn post , Sayedi revealed he’s taking on the role of VP and GM of AMS-Osram’s optical interconnect business line.\",\n   \"- e31 [fact; Ben Wodecki, SDxCentral; original source AMS-Osram ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] AMS-Osram said it has secured an agreement with an unnamed leading AI data-center infrastructure partner for its photonic technology, initially targeting short-distance connections between server racks.\\n    Quote: AMS-Osram is initially targeting its photonic tech for short-distance connections between server racks, with it having already secured an agreement with an unnamed “leading AI data center infrastructure partner.”\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\",\n   \"- e34 [party_statement; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool, recounting Jensen Huang’s statement; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expected Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales from March 2026 through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\",\n   \"- e35 [party_statement; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool, recounting NVIDIA management’s statement; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA announced plans in FY2027 Q1 to expand in CPUs, and management said it expected nearly $20 billion in CPU sales; the item gives no period for that sales estimate.\\n    Quote: Furthermore, in its first fiscal quarter of 2027, Nvidia announced plans to become much more involved in the central processing unit (CPU) space , which has been in high demand due to the rise of agentic AI. Management said they think they can generate nearly $20 billion of CPU sales, making it an instant industry leader.\",\n   \"- e36 [third_party_view; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool, recounting Cerebras’ claim; original source Cerebras ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] Cerebras claimed that its chips were 15 times faster than some NVIDIA GPU models.\\n    Quote: There are competitors like Cerebras and Space Exploration Technologies Corp , which have promised to make more powerful GPUs than Nvidia, and Cerebras already has chips it claims are 15 times faster than some of Nvidia's models.\",\n   \"- e37 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir and NVIDIA ; from gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c 2026-07-03] Palantir is inking a deal to use NVIDIA's Nemotron to build AI models for government; no date or amount was given.\\n    Quote: With Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government,\",\n   \"- e38 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google, Amazon and Tesla feel NVIDIA charges too much.\\n    Quote: The company has some powerful detractors, mainly clients that feel they charge too much, like Google and Amazon and Tesla.\",\n   \"- e39 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google and Amazon claim their chips are better than NVIDIA's, although they use NVIDIA products.\\n    Quote: The first two claim that they have better chips than NVIDIA, even as they use NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027 and $554 billion in FY2028, versus trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e46 [party_statement; Josh Parker; original source Josh Parker, NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA sustainability head Josh Parker said AI compute demand driving data center construction is growing faster than almost any other infrastructure-investment category.\\n    Quote: AI workloads are not getting lighter. The compute demand driving data center construction is growing faster than almost any other category of infrastructure investment.\",\n   \"- e49 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project NVIDIA revenue growth of 82% for FY2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e51 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst Neil Patel; original source Neil Patel 2026-07-04; from gnews:068a24e2743bab750f43f048 2026-07-04] The author calculated that NVIDIA revenue rose 1,033% from Q1 2024 to Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Just in the last three years, from Q1 2024 to the first quarter of fiscal 2027 (ended April 26), Nvidia's revenue soared 1,033%.\",\n   \"- e62 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\",\n   \"- e63 [fact; wccftech.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3faf8050f6d3b8ddee1d18c2 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB has returned to retail shelves.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's GeForce RTX 3060 12 GB has now landed back on retail shelves\",\n   \"- e65 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] NVIDIA forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales in 2026, according to the author.\\n    Quote: Nvidia already forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales this year.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e62 [third_party_view; CNBC, reporting SemiAnalysis’s projection; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis projected NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street consensus.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis also projects Nvidia's data-center compute revenue will run 20% above Wall Street consensus in the second half of fiscal 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e154; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e68 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Humanoid, LG Electronics, NEURA Robotics and Noble Machines ; from nvblog:open-models-icml-2026 2026-07-06] Humanoid, LG Electronics, NEURA Robotics and Noble Machines are adopting NVIDIA Isaac GR00T models for their humanoid deployments; no date or amount was provided.\\n    Quote: Humanoid , LG Electronics , NEURA Robotics and Noble Machines are adopting NVIDIA Isaac GR00T models to accelerate industrial deployments of their humanoids\",\n   \"- e69 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source 1X, Agility, Agile Robots, Boston Dynamics, Hexagon Robotics and Mentee ; from nvblog:open-models-icml-2026 2026-07-06] 1X, Agility, Agile Robots, Boston Dynamics, Hexagon Robotics and Mentee are building humanoids using NVIDIA Cosmos world models, Isaac Sim and Isaac Lab; no date or amount was provided.\\n    Quote: 1X , Agility , Agile Robots , Boston Dynamics , Hexagon Robotics , and Mentee are building the next generation of humanoids using Cosmos world models, Isaac Sim and Isaac Lab to accelerate the development and validation of their robots.\",\n   \"- e73 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis 2026-07-06; from gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said its supply-chain tracking indicates NVIDIA’s second-half 2026 shipment volumes and revenue will be higher than general market estimates.\\n    Quote: Nvidia revenue is skyrocketing, and even 3 years into the build out, the general market is still materially lower on shipment volumes and revenue estimates for Nvidia in the 2nd half of this year versus our through supply chain tracking in the Accelerator Model .\",\n   \"- e81 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley Research estimates the Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscalers about $7.8 million per unit, versus about $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia 's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation.\",\n   \"- e82 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimates NVIDIA will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU at volume.\\n    Quote: The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\",\n   \"- e83 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimates memory content in a Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, up 435% from the prior generation, including 54 terabytes of LPDDR5X and roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.\",\n   \"- e85 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley's bill-of-materials estimates put memory at 25–30% of the VR200 rack, versus 5–10% for the GB200, while the GPU share falls from about 63% to 51%.\\n    Quote: As a share of the bill of materials, memory rose from 5 to 10 percent on the GB200 to 25 to 30 percent on the VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63 percent to 51 percent.\",\n   \"- e86 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimates hyperscalers could reduce the Vera Rubin rack price to around $6.7 million by self-sourcing certain memory modules.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the number.\",\n   \"- e87 [fact; fool.com author Adam Spatacco; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported calendar Q1 2026 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of calendar 2026, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion -- up 85% year over year.\",\n   \"- e88 [fact; fool.com author Adam Spatacco; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported calendar Q1 2026 Data Center segment revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: The company's core data center segment grew even faster, at 92% year over year, to $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expected NVIDIA growth of 82% for the rest of 2026.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth.\",\n   \"- e98 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA and Palantir Technologies 2026-07-06; from gnews:0e3cbf453958ce83fabf7a65 2026-07-06] NVIDIA and Palantir announced a collaboration to bring open AI models into classified environments; no timing or amount was given.\\n    Quote: Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) and Palantir Technologies ( PLTR +1.34% ) announced a collaboration designed to bring powerful open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments.\",\n   \"- e99 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-06; from gnews:0e3cbf453958ce83fabf7a65 2026-07-06] The author estimates that the U.S. government civilian workforce is around 2 million employees across sectors including energy, transportation, healthcare, defense, and financial services.\\n    Quote: The U.S. government civilian workforce is around 2 million employees across critical sectors such as energy, transportation, healthcare, defense, and financial services.\",\n   \"- e100 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in fiscal Q1 2027, or 92% of total sales.\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e122; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e101 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue grew 92% year over year and 21% sequentially in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\",\n   \"- e102 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e104; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e103 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA projected fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e104 [fact; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA revenue was $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: Revenue rose 85% year over year to $81.6 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102, e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: data center up 92% to $75.2 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e88; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e106 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said agentic AI had arrived and was generating value and scaling across companies and industries.\\n    Quote: “Agentic AI has arrived, doing productive work, generating real value and scaling rapidly across companies and industries.”\",\n   \"- e108 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance) 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author estimated NVIDIA had roughly 81% of the AI chip market.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA still owns roughly 81% of the AI chip market\",\n   \"- e109 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\",\n   \"- e110 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance), citing Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast custom ASICs to grow at a 27% CAGR through 2033, versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\",\n   \"- e111 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance), quoting Lisa Su; original source Lisa Su ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] AMD CEO Lisa Su said leading customer forecasts for MI450 exceeded AMD’s initial expectations.\\n    Quote: Lisa Su noted “leading customer forecasts exceeding our initial expectations” on MI450.\",\n   \"- e112 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance) 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author said NVIDIA had $119 billion in supply commitments and judged that they depended on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's $119B in supply commitments hinge on AI delivering measurable economic value beyond productivity tools\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e129; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e113 [fact; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron Q3 revenue was $41.46 billion, up 345.7% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q3 revenue exploded 345.7% year over year to $41.46 billion\",\n   \"- e114 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Micron forecast an adjusted gross margin of 86% for the next quarter.\\n    Quote: Micron is now forecasting adjusted gross margins of 86% next quarter\",\n   \"- e121 [fact; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e104, e156; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e122 [fact; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported data center revenue of $75.25 billion in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: with data center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e100; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e123 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author estimates that hyperscalers account for about 50% of NVIDIA's data center revenue and are funding their own custom chips.\\n    Quote: About 50% of that data center number comes from hyperscalers, the same companies bankrolling Amazon Trainium, Google TPU, Microsoft Maia and Meta MTIA.\",\n   \"- e124 [party_statement; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 total revenue to $91.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e125 [fact; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion\",\n   \"- e126 [fact; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Amazon ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] Amazon disclosed that its Trainium business has reached multi-billion-dollar scale.\\n    Quote: Amazon has disclosed Trainium is now a multi-billion-dollar business\",\n   \"- e127 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero\",\n   \"- e128 [party_statement; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said losing the China data center compute market, which NVIDIA estimates could approach $50 billion in the future, would be material.\\n    Quote: Colette Kress (Nvidia’s CFO) said losing that market, which NVIDIA sizes at “close to about $50 billion in the future,” would be material.\",\n   \"- e129 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author cites $119 billion of NVIDIA supply commitments and says they compound the risk if hyperscaler orders slow.\\n    Quote: Supply commitments of $119 billion compound demand risk if hyperscaler orders slow\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e112; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e131 [fact; Autonocion.com; original source Valar Atomics 2026-07-01; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] On July 1, Valar Atomics powered an Nvidia Blackwell-based desktop unit from its Ward 250 microreactor and served a website using the reactor’s electricity.\\n    Quote: Valar Atomics wired a Blackwell -based Nvidia desktop unit to its Ward 250 microreactor, served a website off the electricity, and announced a plan for something much bigger that skips the local water entirely.\",\n   \"- e132 [third_party_view; Autonocion.com; original source Tom’s Hardware ; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] Tom’s Hardware’s tally said more than 75 US data-center projects worth around $130 billion had been blocked or delayed so far in 2026.\\n    Quote: More than 75 of these projects, worth around $130 billion, have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom’s Hardware .\",\n   \"- e133 [fact; Autonocion.com; original source NVIDIA and Valar Atomics 2026-07-01; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] On July 1, NVIDIA and Valar Atomics announced an agreement to explore nuclear-powered AI systems, including a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah under study.\\n    Quote: Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”\",\n   \"- e134 [fact; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge launched an AI Factory and neocloud offering in Querétaro, Mexico.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge has launched an AI Factory in Querétaro, Mexico, bringing online its neocloud offering.\",\n   \"- e135 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge said its AI Factory platform’s entire initial capacity is contracted to AI-solution companies.\\n    Quote: According to Bleeding Edge, the platform’s entire initial capacity has already been contracted by companies dedicated to developing AI solutions.\",\n   \"- e136 [fact; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge’s neocloud platform incorporates Nvidia Blackwell B300 systems.\\n    Quote: The neocloud platform incorporates Nvidia Blackwell B300 systems and a software layer developed in-house for automation, observability, monitoring, and resource management, with the goal of optimizing workload performance.\",\n   \"- e137 [party_statement; DCD; original source Bleeding Edge ; from gnews:c2924b0380602940d68de7ff 2026-07-06] Bleeding Edge plans in the coming months to expand neocloud and AI Factory capacity, add Nvidia systems, and deploy infrastructure in other markets.\\n    Quote: Bleeding Edge plans to expand both the capacity of its neocloud and its AI Factories in the coming months by incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets.\",\n   \"- e139 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA scrapped the planned NVL72x2 design, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back.\\n    Quote: A planned alternative design called NVL72x2, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, has been scrapped entirely.\",\n   \"- e148 [party_statement; Investing.com, relaying Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein's account of Hon Hai management's forecast; original source Hon Hai management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA's Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\",\n   \"- e154 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis expected NVIDIA data-center compute revenue in the second half of FY2027 to be 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis actually expects Nvidia’s data-center compute revenue in the second half of fiscal 2027 to come in 20% above Wall Street’s current expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e62; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e156 [fact; tikr.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $82 billion and data-center revenue of $75 billion in its most recent quarter; total revenue was up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the most recent quarter, the company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, with data center revenue alone hitting $75 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e166 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] A Bloomberg Intelligence survey said Chinese executives expect domestic products’ share of their AI-accelerator budgets to rise to 46% over the next 12 months from 30% today.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they will allocate 46 per cent of their budget for AI accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months.\",\n   \"- e167 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] In a Bloomberg Intelligence survey, 80% of Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\",\n   \"- e168 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] A large pool of respondents to the Bloomberg Intelligence survey was evaluating AI accelerators from Hygon Information Technology and Cambricon Technologies.\\n    Quote: AI accelerators produced by Hygon Information Technology and Cambricon Technologies were also being evaluated by a large pool of respondents to the survey.\",\n   \"- e169 [third_party_view; Bloomberg Intelligence report, quoted by businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence said China’s substitution of locally made AI semiconductors for foreign ones was making progress and was likely to benefit domestic makers such as Huawei and Hygon; its survey covered 60 executives.\\n    Quote: “China’s drive to substitute locally-made AI semiconductors for foreign ones is making progress, which is likely to benefit domestic makers such as Huawei and Hygon,” said the report, which surveyed 60 executives at Chinese software, finance, manufacturing and retail companies.\",\n   \"- e170 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] A Bloomberg Intelligence survey expected Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local firms took over, noting Beijing had urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\",\n   \"- e171 [fact; businesstimes.com.sg; original source China ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centers over the next five years as part of a government-led AI expansion initiative.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly two trillion yuan (US$294 billion) to build data centres across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand the use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\",\n   \"- e172 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies would supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-center initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\",\n   \"- e173 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence report ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] The report said a global memory-chip shortage was likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC and that bottlenecks were shifting toward securing high-bandwidth memory supply.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corporation, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to reap the benefits.\",\n   \"- e37 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir and NVIDIA ; from gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c 2026-07-03] Palantir is inking a deal to use NVIDIA's Nemotron to build AI models for government; no date or amount was given.\\n    Quote: With Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e176; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: data center up 92% to $75.2 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e88, e199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e109 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% above the year-earlier quarter.\\n    Quote: Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e202; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e110 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance), citing Bloomberg Intelligence; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast custom ASICs to grow at a 27% CAGR through 2033, versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasting a 27% CAGR for custom ASICs through 2033 versus 16% for AI accelerators.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e203; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e127 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan 2026-07-06; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] The author says NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero.\\n    Quote: China data center compute revenue is effectively zero\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e209; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e174 [third_party_view; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Perplexity ; from nvblog:nvidia-vera-max-single-threaded-cpu-at-scale 2026-07-07] Perplexity is looking to deploy NVIDIA Vera in an upcoming production system; no date or scale was specified.\\n    Quote: Perplexity is now looking to deploy Vera in its upcoming production system.\",\n   \"- e175 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face 2026-07-07; from nvblog:hugging-face-lerobot-models-frameworks-open-robotics 2026-07-07] NVIDIA and Hugging Face announced integrations of Isaac GR00T 1.7 and Isaac Teleop with LeRobot, with Cosmos 3 planned for LeRobot soon.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA and Hugging Face are collaborating to bring the NVIDIA Isaac GR00T 1.7 open, reasoning vision language action (VLA) model for humanoid robots and the NVIDIA Isaac Teleop framework to LeRobot — Hugging Face’s open source library for robotics — with NVIDIA Cosmos 3 , a frontier model for physical AI, planned soon.\",\n   \"- e176 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Palantir Technologies Inc. ; from gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1 2026-07-07] Palantir announced it is combining its new intelligence engine with NVIDIA Nemotron models to deliver AI for U.S. government agencies and major infrastructure operators.\\n    Quote: Earlier this week, Palantir announced that it is combining its new intelligence engine and Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI for government agencies and major infrastructure operators in the U.S.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e37; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e180 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source finance.yahoo.com ; from gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677 2026-07-07] The article said NVIDIA faces rising competition from specialized AI chips as Amazon and Alphabet extend access to their in-house processors.\\n    Quote: The move comes as the company faces rising competition from specialized AI chips from cloud providers, including Amazon and Alphabet, which are extending access to in-house processors.\",\n   \"- e181 [party_statement; NVIDIA, in a company blog post by Edith Llontop and Brandon Neel; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-07; from gnews:56085a9d3e88c464bcaed67b 2026-07-07] NVIDIA said 1X, Agility, ANYBotics, Bellboy Robotics, FieldAI, Lightwheel AI, NEURA Robotics, Nexuni, Noble Machines, Schaeffler, Skild AI, and Techman Robot are integrating GR00T platform components into their development pipelines.\\n    Quote: Humanoid makers and AI providers including 1X, Agility, ANYBotics, Bellboy Robotics, FieldAI, Lightwheel AI, NEURA Robotics, Nexuni, Noble Machines, Schaeffler, Skild AI, and Techman Robot are integrating components of the GR00T platform such as Isaac Teleop, Sim, Lab, and ROS to accelerate their development pipeline and bring AI-enabled robots into real industrial use faster.\",\n   \"- e186 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author says NVIDIA sales will likely accelerate as data-center spending shifts from construction costs to computing costs.\\n    Quote: There's a very strong correlation between increasing data center spending and Nvidia's sales, and that trend will likely accelerate as data centers shift from construction costs to computing costs.\",\n   \"- e187 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author expects Microsoft and TSMC to report strong earnings and forward guidance, which the author says could lift NVIDIA shares.\\n    Quote: I think both of these companies will report strong earnings with great forward guidance, and that could cause Nvidia's stock to rise.\",\n   \"- e188 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author says NVIDIA's core clients have not shifted their actual spending habits and expects NVIDIA to report a strong quarter in late August.\\n    Quote: Even if it doesn't, Nvidia reports earnings in late August and will likely report another blowout quarter, as there hasn't been any shift in actual spending habits from Nvidia's core clients yet.\",\n   \"- e189 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:784c556d2e58ed09dd8aa7fc 2026-07-07] NVIDIA reported automotive revenue rose 39% year over year in FY2026, driven by adoption of its self-driving platforms.\\n    Quote: In its latest annual filing, Nvidia reported automotive revenue for fiscal year 2026 was up 39% from a year prior, driven by the adoption of its self-driving platforms.\",\n   \"- e194 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author forecast that new capacity across much of the memory industry would not come online until 2027 or later, leaving low inventory supply for at least 18 months and potentially pushing memory-chip prices higher.\\n    Quote: new capacity for many in this industry won't be online until 2027 or later, creating a low supply of inventory for at least the next year and a half. That could lead to even higher memory chip prices\",\n   \"- e195 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author expected DRAM sales growth to track GPU-demand growth at a similar rate.\\n    Quote: since DRAM will likely grow at a similar rate to GPU demand.\",\n   \"- e199 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e201 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom reported Q2 AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q2 AI semiconductor revenue was $10.8 billion, +143% YoY,\",\n   \"- e202 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Broadcom guided Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion.\\n    Quote: with Q3 guided to $16.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e203 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Bloomberg Intelligence forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts 27% CAGR for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e110; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e204 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, while its backlog nearly doubled to more than $460 billion.\\n    Quote: Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion,\",\n   \"- e206 [rumour; mlq.ai; original source DeepSeek, as reported by Reuters citing three unnamed sources ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip, according to a Reuters report citing three sources; no production date was disclosed.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek is developing a custom chip designed for AI inference — generating model responses — rather than training, Reuters reported citing three sources [1]\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e213; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e207 [rumour; mlq.ai; original source DeepSeek, as reported by Reuters citing people with knowledge of the matter ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek’s custom-chip project has been underway for roughly a year; the company has expanded its chip engineering team and is discussing the project with chip-design firms, foundries, and memory suppliers.\\n    Quote: The project has been underway for roughly a year and remains in early stages, with DeepSeek quietly expanding its chip engineering team without public job postings [2] . The company is in discussions with chip design firms, semiconductor foundries, and memory suppliers, though no specific partners have been named.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e214, e215; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e208 [fact; mlq.ai; original source DeepSeek ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek closed a $7.5 billion funding round at a valuation above $50 billion, its first outside capital raise, with backing from Tencent, CATL, and founder Liang Wenfeng.\\n    Quote: It comes weeks after the company closed a record $7.5 billion funding round — its first outside capital — at a valuation exceeding $50 billion, with backing from Tencent, CATL, and founder Liang Wenfeng himself [4] .\",\n   \"- e209 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Richard Windey ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windey said U.S. export rules have effectively eliminated Nvidia’s China revenue and also limit DeepSeek’s ability to manufacture or sell advanced chips outside China.\\n    Quote: Analyst Richard Windey highlighted the constraint: the same export rules that have effectively zeroed out Nvidia's China revenue also limit DeepSeek's ability to manufacture or sell advanced silicon outside China [3].\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e127, e216; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e210 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Industry surveys, as reported by mlq.ai ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to allocate 46% of AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Industry surveys indicate Chinese firms plan to shift 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic suppliers within 12 months, up from roughly 30% today [5] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e166; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e211 [fact; Nebius; original source LangChain 2026-07-07; from gnews:022516991251df7f1af4d7cb 2026-07-07] LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra on 2026-07-07; the profile is reported to achieve top agent accuracy among open models at roughly 10x lower cost than closed alternatives.\\n    Quote: Today, LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, achieving top agent accuracy among open models at roughly 10x lower cost than closed alternatives, with no changes to the model itself.\",\n   \"- e212 [fact; Nebius; original source Nebius and LangChain 2026-07-07; from gnews:022516991251df7f1af4d7cb 2026-07-07] Nebius and LangChain partnered to integrate Nebius Token Factory with LangChain’s Deep Agents; the item reports the integration on 2026-07-07.\\n    Quote: Nebius and LangChain have partnered to integrate Nebius Token Factory with LangChain’s Deep Agents.\",\n   \"- e213 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Three unnamed sources familiar with DeepSeek's plans, as reported by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Three Reuters sources said DeepSeek is designing its own AI chips specifically for inference.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e206; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e214 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Reuters sources familiar with DeepSeek's plans ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Reuters sources said DeepSeek has communicated with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers over the past year to support its chip development.\\n    Quote: Over the past year, the company has been communicating with chip design firms, foundries and memory suppliers to support the development of the semiconductors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e207; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e215 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Reuters sources familiar with DeepSeek's plans ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Reuters sources said DeepSeek increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek has also increased recruitment of chip design engineers in recent months.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e207; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e216 [third_party_view; Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windsor said Nvidia's position in China is effectively zero and will remain so, and that DeepSeek is unlikely to sell chips outside China without access to advanced manufacturing technology.\\n    Quote: \\\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\\\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e209; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e217 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source Huawei ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Huawei now controls around half of China's AI chip market, valued at approximately US$50 billion.\\n    Quote: Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\",\n   \"- e218 [fact; idnfinancials.com; original source OpenAI and Broadcom ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, Jalapeno, in collaboration with Broadcom last month.\\n    Quote: OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, while Anthropic is also reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.\",\n   \"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027 and $554 billion in FY2028, versus trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49, e226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102, e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e167 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] In a Bloomberg Intelligence survey, 80% of Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80 per cent of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e242; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e170 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] A Bloomberg Intelligence survey expected Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local firms took over, noting Beijing had urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e243; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e172 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies would supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-center initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80 per cent of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e175 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face 2026-07-07; from nvblog:hugging-face-lerobot-models-frameworks-open-robotics 2026-07-07] NVIDIA and Hugging Face announced integrations of Isaac GR00T 1.7 and Isaac Teleop with LeRobot, with Cosmos 3 planned for LeRobot soon.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA and Hugging Face are collaborating to bring the NVIDIA Isaac GR00T 1.7 open, reasoning vision language action (VLA) model for humanoid robots and the NVIDIA Isaac Teleop framework to LeRobot — Hugging Face’s open source library for robotics — with NVIDIA Cosmos 3 , a frontier model for physical AI, planned soon.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e248, e249, e250; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e199 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue reached $75.246 billion (+92% YoY) in Q1 FY27,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e247; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e211 [fact; Nebius; original source LangChain 2026-07-07; from gnews:022516991251df7f1af4d7cb 2026-07-07] LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra on 2026-07-07; the profile is reported to achieve top agent accuracy among open models at roughly 10x lower cost than closed alternatives.\\n    Quote: Today, LangChain released a Deep Agents profile tuned for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, achieving top agent accuracy among open models at roughly 10x lower cost than closed alternatives, with no changes to the model itself.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e219; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e219 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source LangChain ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] LangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra; the item reports the integration and its benchmark results, including 10x lower inference cost per run than leading closed models.\\n    Quote: LangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, achieving the highest accuracy among open models, while completing more tasks at higher throughput and running at 10x lower inference cost per run than leading closed models.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e211; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e220 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source EY; Abridge; Amdocs; Box ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents; Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents into their platforms.\\n    Quote: Abridge, Amdocs and Box are embedding specialized agents directly into their platforms and global systems integrator EY is expanding its NVIDIA implementation capabilities around NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints for LangChain Deep Agents, helping clients customize, evaluate and govern specialized agents across high-value workflows.\",\n   \"- e221 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source Baseten; Crusoe Cloud; DeepInfra; Fireworks; Nebius; Together AI ; from nvblog:nemotron-langchain-agents-open-stack 2026-07-08] LangChain developers can access NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra through Baseten, Crusoe Cloud, DeepInfra, Fireworks, Nebius and Together AI platforms, providing a hosted path to the tuned harness.\\n    Quote: LangChain developers can access Nemotron 3 Ultra on Baseten , Crusoe Cloud , DeepInfra, Fireworks , Nebius and Together AI platforms, giving them a direct, hosted path to the tuned harness in production.\",\n   \"- e222 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported on July 8, citing unnamed sources, that Chinese officials told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they could seek approval to buy limited quantities of NVIDIA H200 chips, subject to stating the quantity and reason for purchase.\\n    Quote: China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia, a sign the country is easing restrictions on the coveted US technology, according to the Information news site. Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to devel\",\n   \"- e223 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported on July 8, citing unnamed sources, that China was still determining the permitted H200 purchase quantity and the total could be fewer than 200,000 chips.\\n    Quote: The Chinese government, meanwhile, is still figuring out how many H200 chips to allow the companies to buy, but the total may end up being fewer than 200,000, the Information reported.\",\n   \"- e226 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Unnamed analysts ; from gnews:b40db2c507df72ec016e99e6 2026-07-08] Analysts expect NVIDIA total revenue of $392.7 billion in FY2027.\\n    Quote: And analysts are anticipating further gains of $392.7 billion in its current fiscal year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e227 [rumour; thenextweb.com; original source The Information ; from gnews:c2ccca1a61b99adc685b1aa2 2026-07-08] NVIDIA and d-Matrix plan to ship a joint AI-inference system, with Parasail as its first customer and the system due online later in 2026.\\n    Quote: The GPU giant is combining its hardware with inference chips from the startup d-Matrix , The Information reported. The two will ship a joint system to run AI models. The AI-cloud firm Parasail will be its first customer, with the system due online later this year.\",\n   \"- e228 [fact; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-08; from gnews:f7a5bf37167c4f05c3585a2f 2026-07-08] NVIDIA said GPU-accelerated Presto is integrated into IBM watsonx.data and ready for production-workload testing.\\n    Quote: With integration in the IBM watsonx.data platform, GPU-accelerated Presto is now ready for testing on your production workloads.\",\n   \"- e229 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com author; original source Analysts ; from gnews:bbb38537c01d8be774edc057 2026-07-08] Analysts forecast NVIDIA will have one of the strongest revenue growth rates among large-cap companies in 2026.\\n    Quote: Nvidia remains among the fastest-growing large-cap companies, with analysts forecasting one of the strongest revenue expansion rates in the index this year.\",\n   \"- e233 [fact; Futuriom; original source Meta 2026-07-01; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models on July 1, 2026.\\n    Quote: On July 1, the same day NVIDIA announced its new revenue-sharing model, Bloomberg reported that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business selling AI compute and models.\",\n   \"- e237 [fact; CNBC; original source SambaNova 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] SambaNova raised $1 billion in financing, valuing it at $11 billion; General Atlantic led the round, with Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group participating.\\n    Quote: SambaNova is now valued at $11 billion thanks to the financing, which was led by General Atlantic along with participation from Seligman Ventures, T. Rowe Price and Capital Group.\",\n   \"- e238 [fact; CNBC; original source JPMorgan Chase 2026-07-08; from gnews:6b89157155648b9ec317d209 2026-07-08] JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova systems for on-prem inference in its enterprise AI workloads.\\n    Quote: On Wednesday, JPMorgan Chase said it would deploy SambaNova's systems for \\\"on-prem inference in our demanding enterprise AI workloads.\\\"\",\n   \"- e239 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg-tracked analysts ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg-tracked analyst estimates put NVIDIA FY2027 profit at $228 billion, up 90%, and sales at $393 billion, up 82%; the profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\\n    Quote: company is projected to generate $228 billion in profit on $393 billion in sales in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31, representing expected growth of 90% and 82%, respectively, while its profit estimate has risen 13% over the past three months.\",\n   \"- e240 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited by the outlet put NVIDIA's share of the server GPU market at 97% at end-2025, up from 95% at end-2024.\\n    Quote: the company holding 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source.\",\n   \"- e241 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting a Bloomberg Intelligence survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] A Bloomberg Intelligence survey of Chinese executives found they expect domestic products to receive 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e166; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e242 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting a Bloomberg Intelligence survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence survey respondents 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] In a Bloomberg Intelligence survey, 80% of Chinese executives said their total infrastructure spending was running over budget in 2026, mostly because of AI-project costs.\\n    Quote: In addition, 80% of executives said their total infrastructure spending is running over-budget this year, mostly because of the high cost of AI-related projects.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e167; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e243 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting a Bloomberg Intelligence survey; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] A Bloomberg Intelligence survey expects Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and local suppliers gain ground.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use, become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e170; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e244 [fact; Bloomberg, citing Bloomberg News; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) over five years to build data centers, with domestic companies expected to supply at least 80% of core technologies such as chips.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management. At least 80% of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e172; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e245 [third_party_view; Vivek Arya, as quoted by uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source Vivek Arya 2026-07-08; from gnews:266c882eea8c686ee7aafac7 2026-07-08] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said NVIDIA sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year on year, nearly twice cloud capital-expenditure growth; the period was not specified.\\n    Quote: Sales to hyperscalers rose 115% year-on-year, nearly twice cloud capex growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e254; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; QZ; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e247 [fact; QZ; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA's data center segment reported record revenue of $75.2 billion in fiscal Q1 2027.\\n    Quote: its data center segment set a record at $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e248 [fact; The Robot Report Staff; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face ; from gnews:3c9107e3970ce72baf8bb11a 2026-07-08] NVIDIA and Hugging Face are integrating NVIDIA Isaac GR00T 1.7 and Isaac Teleop into Hugging Face’s LeRobot robotics library.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA and Hugging Face are collaborating to bring the NVIDIA Isaac GR00T 1.7 and the NVIDIA Isaac Teleop framework to LeRobot, Hugging Face’s open-source robotics library.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e249 [party_statement; The Robot Report Staff, reporting the companies’ statement; original source NVIDIA and Hugging Face ; from gnews:3c9107e3970ce72baf8bb11a 2026-07-08] NVIDIA and Hugging Face said they hope to bring NVIDIA Cosmos 3 to the LeRobot platform soon.\\n    Quote: The companies said they hope to bring NVIDIA Cosmos 3, a frontier model for physical AI, to the platform soon.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e250 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source Nvidia and Hugging Face 2026-07-06; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Nvidia and Hugging Face added Nvidia’s Isaac GR00T 1.7 models and Isaac Teleop framework to LeRobot on July 6, and plan to integrate Cosmos 3 in the future.\\n    Quote: Under the deal, unveiled on July 6, the companies added Nvidia's Isaac GR00T 1.7 open reasoning vision-language-action (VLA) models for humanoid robotics and the Isaac Teleop framework for robotics data collection into LeRobot, with the Cosmos 3 frontier robotics model planned for future integration.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e175; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e251 [third_party_view; aibusiness.com; original source Lian Jye Su, Omdia ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Omdia analyst Lian Jye Su said Nvidia is facing challenges from Chinese vendors as humanoid robotics vendors rise in China.\\n    Quote: “The company is facing some challenges from Chinese vendors due to the rise of humanoid robotics vendors in China ,” Su noted.\",\n   \"- e252 [fact; aibusiness.com; original source aibusiness.com ; from gnews:21e9182d07508a6690f10419 2026-07-08] Qualcomm’s Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel’s OpenVINO robotics offerings have recently entered the market to challenge Nvidia’s position.\\n    Quote: In addition, Qualcomm, with its Dragonwing IQ10 and Intel, with its OpenVINO robotics offerings, have recently entered the fold to challenge Nvidia’s position.\",\n   \"- e254 [third_party_view; moomoo.com; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42 2026-07-08] Bank of America said NVIDIA’s hyperscaler sales increased 115% year over year, nearly twice the growth in cloud capital expenditures.\\n    Quote: The report also says Nvidia’s hyperscaler sales rose 115% year over year, nearly twice cloud capex growth, suggesting wallet-share gains rather than share loss.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e245; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e255 [fact; Parasail and d-Matrix, in a joint press release distributed by PR Newswire; original source Parasail 2026-07-08; from gnews:040c256543fc8106ffecabae 2026-07-08] Parasail announced it is deploying d-Matrix Corsair accelerators alongside its NVIDIA Hopper and Blackwell architectures for inference services.\\n    Quote: Parasail, the inference cloud for AI-native startups, and d-Matrix, a pioneer in low-latency AI inference compute platforms for data centers, today announced Parasail is deploying d-Matrix Corsair inference accelerators alongside the NVIDIA Hopper and NVIDIA Blackwell architectures to deliver up to 10x faster, more cost-efficient inference services to its customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e227 (); both are in force: NVIDIA and d-Matrix plan to ship a joint AI-inference system, with Parasail as its first customer and the system due online later in 2026.\",\n   \"- e256 [fact; larsentoubro.com; original source L&T Vyoma and Fortanix 2026-07-08; from gnews:79b4840d3de4aa77ec0d0229 2026-07-08] L&T Vyoma entered a partnership with Fortanix to jointly deliver sovereign, secure SaaS offerings in India, using NVIDIA Confidential Computing as part of the offering.\\n    Quote: Larsen & Toubro Vyoma (L&T Vyoma), L&T’s next-generation sovereign AI cloud and digital infrastructure business, has entered a strategic partnership with Fortanix Inc, a US-headquartered global leader in data and AI security and a pioneer in Confidential Computing. They will jointly deliver sovereign, secure software-as-a-service offerings for enterprises and government organisations in India.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102, e246, e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e34 [party_statement; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool, recounting Jensen Huang’s statement; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expected Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales from March 2026 through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e281; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e102 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e104, e270; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e103 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA projected fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124, e274; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: data center up 92% to $75.2 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e88, e199, e271; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e125 [fact; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: Networking revenue grew 199% year over year to $14.8 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e272; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e206 [rumour; mlq.ai; original source DeepSeek, as reported by Reuters citing three unnamed sources ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek is developing a custom AI inference chip, according to a Reuters report citing three sources; no production date was disclosed.\\n    Quote: DeepSeek is developing a custom chip designed for AI inference — generating model responses — rather than training, Reuters reported citing three sources [1]\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e213, e264; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e207 [rumour; mlq.ai; original source DeepSeek, as reported by Reuters citing people with knowledge of the matter ; from gnews:9f430c6ce2e8d551fe1f063a 2026-07-07] DeepSeek’s custom-chip project has been underway for roughly a year; the company has expanded its chip engineering team and is discussing the project with chip-design firms, foundries, and memory suppliers.\\n    Quote: The project has been underway for roughly a year and remains in early stages, with DeepSeek quietly expanding its chip engineering team without public job postings [2] . The company is in discussions with chip design firms, semiconductor foundries, and memory suppliers, though no specific partners have been named.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e214, e215, e265; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e222 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported on July 8, citing unnamed sources, that Chinese officials told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they could seek approval to buy limited quantities of NVIDIA H200 chips, subject to stating the quantity and reason for purchase.\\n    Quote: China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia, a sign the country is easing restrictions on the coveted US technology, according to the Information news site. Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to devel\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e284, e301; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; QZ; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e269; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e257 [fact; FEV Group, in a release carried by Vietnam Investment Review; original source FEV and Microsoft 2026-07-09; from gnews:c8324bfbfe7f0c60c826e72f 2026-07-09] FEV and Microsoft announced a collaboration to integrate in-vehicle generative AI built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices; no period or amount was stated.\\n    Quote: FEV is collaborating with Microsoft to integrate powerful, in-vehicle Generative AI capabilities built on NVIDIA GPU-accelerated compute and AI model microservices.\",\n   \"- e258 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The author says demand for high-bandwidth memory is growing faster than supply can scale, allowing memory companies to raise prices tenfold over the past year.\\n    Quote: since demand is growing faster than anyone can scale up supply, they have been able to increase prices tenfold over the past year.\",\n   \"- e259 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The author says the GPU shortage has eased somewhat since last year.\\n    Quote: The GPU shortage that looked so alarming last year has eased off a bit.\",\n   \"- e260 [third_party_view; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source TechCrunch author Russell Brandom 2026-07-09; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] The author says the spot price for an hour of Nvidia H100 GPU compute peaked at around $3.20 in May 2026 and then steadily declined.\\n    Quote: there’s a peak in May (around $3.20 an hour) and then a steady drop-off.\",\n   \"- e261 [fact; TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source Google, Amazon, Microsoft and OpenAI ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Google, Amazon, Microsoft and OpenAI have launched custom processors intended to reduce their dependence on Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Google , Amazon , Microsoft , and even OpenAI have launched their own custom processors to lessen their dependence on Nvidia\",\n   \"- e262 [third_party_view; Wayne Nelms, quoted by TechCrunch author Russell Brandom; original source Wayne Nelms ; from gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec 2026-07-09] Ornn co-founder and CTO Wayne Nelms says GPU and accelerator competition is increasing while companies are not making their own DRAM, and expects current market conditions to persist absent a major HBM breakthrough, a supply-and-demand shift or a new memory entrant.\\n    Quote: “More GPU and accelerator players are entering the market. Everyone wants to make their own silicon, but no one is making their own DRAM,” Nelms told me. “Until there’s a major technological breakthrough on HBM [high-bandwidth memory], a shift in supply and demand, or someone new [enters the market in memory], I think things will more or less persist as we see today.”\",\n   \"- e263 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance, quoting Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya ; from gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf 2026-07-09] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said concerns weighing on NVIDIA included gross-margin pressure from higher memory costs, custom-ASIC competition, crowded investor ownership, and cash used for vendor financing instead of stronger shareholder returns.\\n    Quote: Several concerns are fueling the sell-off, Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya wrote in a note this week. They include gross margin pressure from higher memory costs, competition from custom ASIC chips, crowded investor ownership, and unproductive use of cash in vendor financing rather than stronger buybacks/dividends.\",\n   \"- e264 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] DeepSeek is reportedly developing an inference-focused AI chip, which could reduce its reliance on NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Reports that DeepSeek is developing its own inference-focused AI chip could reduce its reliance on Nvidia's GPUs\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e206; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e265 [rumour; barchart.com; original source DeepSeek ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] DeepSeek is engaging chip-design, foundry, and memory partners and expanding its chip engineering team for its inference-chip project.\\n    Quote: the company engaging chip design, foundry, and memory partners while quietly expanding its chip engineering team\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e207; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e266 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source unnamed experts ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Experts said DeepSeek's chip project is unlikely to materially affect NVIDIA's near-term revenue, citing China's shrinking contribution to NVIDIA sales.\\n    Quote: experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales\",\n   \"- e267 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] The author said custom silicon could gradually erode NVIDIA's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\",\n   \"- e269 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e270 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140% year over year, and non-GAAP gross margin of 75%, versus 60.8% a year earlier.\\n    Quote: On a non-GAAP basis, earnings per share (EPS) rose 140% from the prior-year period to $1.87, beating analyst estimates. Non-GAAP gross margin expanded to 75% from 60.8% a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e271 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA Data Center revenue reached a record $75.2 billion in fiscal 2027's first quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: the Data Center segment remained Nvidia's biggest growth driver, with revenue surging 92% YOY to a record $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e279; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e272 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027's first quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e125; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e273 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA Edge Computing revenue was $6.4 billion in fiscal 2027's first quarter, up 29% year over year.\\n    Quote: Its Edge Computing revenue increased 29% YOY to $6.4 billion\",\n   \"- e274 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA guided to fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%, assuming no China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%. The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e275 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source analysts ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Analysts forecast NVIDIA EPS of $8.69 in fiscal 2027, up 90.2%, and $11.67 in fiscal 2028, up 34.3%.\\n    Quote: Street expects Nvidia's momentum to continue, with analysts forecasting EPS growth of 90.2% YOY to $8.69 in fiscal 2027, followed by another 34.3% increase to $11.67 in fiscal 2028.\",\n   \"- e276 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Morgan Stanley maintained its $288 NVIDIA price target and Overweight rating in June 2026.\\n    Quote: Last month, Morgan Stanley reaffirmed its \\\"Overweight\\\" rating on the stock and maintained its $288 price target\",\n   \"- e277 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Truist Securities ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Truist Securities reiterated its $307 NVIDIA price target and Buy rating after NVIDIA unveiled next-generation AI products at GTC Taipei.\\n    Quote: Truist Securities reiterated its \\\"Buy\\\" rating and $307 price target after Nvidia unveiled several next-generation AI products at GTC Taipei.\",\n   \"- e278 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] The article reported an average NVIDIA analyst price target of $301.92 and a Street-high target of $500.\\n    Quote: The average analyst price target for NVDA is $301.92, indicating a potential upside of 47.9%. Also, the Street-high target price of $500 suggests that the stock could rally as much as 145%.\",\n   \"- e279 [fact; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported record data center segment revenue in the first quarter.\\n    Quote: Revenues from Nvidia's data center segment -- the primary engine of the business -- set a record in the first quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e271; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e280 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management guided to faster data center segment revenue growth in the second quarter.\\n    Quote: management guided for further revenue growth acceleration for the second quarter.\",\n   \"- e281 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e282 [fact; Rick Munarriz, Fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] NVIDIA revenue accelerated for three consecutive quarters, and revenue rose 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 FY2027, its strongest increase in 18 months.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters. The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e283 [third_party_view; Rick Munarriz, Fool.com; original source Rick Munarriz 2026-07-09; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] Fool.com analyst Rick Munarriz judged that demand for NVIDIA products was growing faster than competition and trade restrictions were increasing.\\n    Quote: Demand is outpacing the uptick in competitors and trade restrictions.\",\n   \"- e288 [third_party_view; QZ.com; original source QZ.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon could introduce its Trainium4 AI chip later in 2026.\\n    Quote: Amazon 's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\",\n   \"- e289 [fact; QZ.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 300 chip is in production for ranking and recommendation work.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work.\",\n   \"- e290 [third_party_view; QZ.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta plans to build three more MTIA chip generations over the next two years to run generative AI models.\\n    Quote: Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e293 [party_statement; QZ.com; original source OpenAI ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI plans to begin installing its jointly developed 10-gigawatt custom AI chips in the second half of 2026, with installations continuing through 2029.\\n    Quote: Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\",\n   \"- e296 [fact; QZ.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Broadcom reported $5.2 billion of AI-related revenue in fiscal 2025's third quarter.\\n    Quote: The company reported $5.2 billion in AI-related revenue for the third quarter of its 2025 fiscal year.\",\n   \"- e297 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta Platforms 2026-07-09; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026, according to a Reuters report citing an internal memo.\\n    Quote: $Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\",\n   \"- e298 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta’s monthly sales more than doubled year over year to NT$385.19 billion in June 2026; Quanta supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e299 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Hon Hai’s monthly sales rose 52% year over year to NT$821.8 billion in June 2026; Hon Hai is an Nvidia server-assembly partner.\\n    Quote: $HON HAI PRECISION INDUSTRY SPON GDS EACH REP 2 SHS TWD10 REG'S' (HNHPF.US)$ , Nvidia’s server assembly partner, saw a 52% surge in monthly sales in June to NT$ 821.8 billion\",\n   \"- e300 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Hon Hai’s quarterly sales rose 40%, more than expected; the item does not specify the quarter’s dates or sales amount.\\n    Quote: allowing the Taiwanese company to post a bigger-than-expected 40% surge in quarterly sales, according to Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e65 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] NVIDIA forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales in 2026, according to the author.\\n    Quote: Nvidia already forecasts $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e334; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e102 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.87, up 140%.\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e104, e270, e307; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e105 [fact; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year; the item does not specify the reporting period.\\n    Quote: data center up 92% to $75.2 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e88, e199, e271, e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e124 [party_statement; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management guided Q2 FY2027 total revenue to $91.0 billion.\\n    Quote: Management guided Q2 FY27 revenue to $91.0 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103, e312; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  