ding 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e304; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e272 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA Data Center networking revenue was $14.8 billion in fiscal 2027's first quarter, up 199% year over year; Data Center computing revenue was $60.4 billion.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking revenue soared 199% YOY to $14.8 billion, while computing revenue accounted for the remaining $60.4 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e125, e318; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e282 [fact; Rick Munarriz, Fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b412380d12c5a222545d42f1 2026-07-09] NVIDIA revenue accelerated for three consecutive quarters, and revenue rose 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 FY2027, its strongest increase in 18 months.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue has accelerated for three consecutive quarters. The 85% top-line jump it posted in its fiscal first quarter is the strongest increase in a year and a half.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e332; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e297 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source Meta Platforms 2026-07-09; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Meta reportedly plans to start manufacturing its AI chip in September 2026, according to a Reuters report citing an internal memo.\\n    Quote: $Meta Platforms (META.US)$ is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its AI chip in September, Reuters reported Thursday, citing the company’s internal memo.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e308; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e304 [