r after completing initial testing.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e297; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e309 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Meta Platforms ; from gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7 2026-07-10] Meta's planned Iris AI processor is being designed with Broadcom and manufactured by TSMC.\\n    Quote: The chip is being designed with Broadcom (AVGO) and manufactured by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (TSM).\",\n   \"- e310 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Meta Platforms ; from gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7 2026-07-10] Meta's Iris processor is intended to support its AI infrastructure and complement, not replace, the large number of GPUs it continues to buy from Nvidia and AMD.\\n    Quote: The report said the processor is intended to support Meta's AI infrastructure while complementing, rather than replacing, the large number of graphics processors the company continues to buy from Nvidia and Advanced Micro Devices (AMD).\",\n   \"- e311 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e312 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124, e319; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e313 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 guidance excluded Data Center compute revenue from China; the company reported zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance explicitly excludes Data Center compute revenue from China, and there were zero H20 shipments in the quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e320; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e314 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author cites NVIDIA revenue growth of 85.23% year over year and a 75.0% non-GAAP gross margin.\\n    Quote: For a business growing revenue 85.23% year over year at 75.0% non-GAAP gross margins, that is cheap on any historical comparison.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e315 [rumour; GuruFocus; original source GuruFocus ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] The article reports rumors that Meta and other major NVIDIA clients are developing their own AI chips, which could affect NVIDIA's market share.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's stock surge comes amidst growing concerns that major clients, such as Meta, are shifting towards developing their own AI chips.\",\n   \"- e317 [fact; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 results put hard numbers behind the moat argument. The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e318 [fact; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier, reflecting surging demand for the Spectrum-X Ethernet and NVLink interconnect systems that travel with every rack-scale Blackwell deployment.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e272; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e319 [party_statement; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e312; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA management (outlook assumption); David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St. (upside interpretation) ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China; the author says a policy change permitting H200 exports could add upside.\\n    Quote: Notably, that outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China, meaning any policy thaw on H200 exports could represent additional upside.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e313; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e321 [fact; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source OpenAI, Anthropic, Meta Platforms, Oracle, and xAI ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] OpenAI, Anthropic, Meta, Oracle, and xAI have deployment commitments for NVIDIA's Blackwell and Vera Rubin platforms; the article gives no amounts or dates.\\n    Quote: Deployment commitments from OpenAI, Anthropic, Meta Platforms ( NASDAQ:META ), Oracle ( NYSE:ORCL ), and xAI translate that framing into tangible order flow for NVIDIA’s Blackwell and Vera Rubin platforms.\",\n   \"- e322 [third_party_view; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA (FY2026 revenue); David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St. (growth interpretation) ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] The author cites NVIDIA FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion and argues that sustaining comparable percentage growth from that base becomes harder.\\n    Quote: A cheaper forward multiple on NVIDIA can reflect a rational market pricing in decelerating growth off an enormous revenue base. NVIDIA’s FY2026 revenue reached $215.9 billion, and sustaining comparable percentage growth becomes mathematically harder from that starting point.\",\n   \"- e323 [fact; theverge.com; original source Counterpoint ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Counterpoint reported that in June 2026 SK Hynix held 29% of the global DRAM market, versus Samsung at 38% and Micron at 22%.\\n    Quote: As of June 2026, SK Hynix makes up 29 percent of the global DRAM market, with Samsung at 38 percent and Micron at 22 percent, according to data from Counterpoint .\",\n   \"- e324 [party_statement; theverge.com; original source SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said SK Hynix plans to increase memory-chip capacity over the five years after June 2026 to address a shortage he said could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years to address a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\",\n   \"- e325 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos, as quoted by 24/7 Wall St.; original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] CNBC’s Kristina Partsinevelos said SK Hynix holds roughly 58% of the high-bandwidth memory market, while Micron and Samsung each hold roughly 21%, citing Counterpoint Research.\\n    Quote: “SK Hynix is the world leader in high bandwidth memory . The memory that feeds AI chips with roughly 58% of that market. Micron and Samsung competitors split roughly 21% each … as per Counterpoint Research.”\",\n   \"- e326 [third_party_view; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said SK Hynix revenue is expected to triple to $235 billion this year and that the company is committing over $720 billion in capital investment over the coming years, primarily in South Korea.\\n    Quote: Partsinevelos noted revenue is expected to triple to $235 billion this year, with the company committing over $720 billion in capital investment over the coming years, primarily in South Korea.\",\n   \"- e327 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos, as quoted by 24/7 Wall St.; original source Kristina Partsinevelos 2026-07-10; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Kristina Partsinevelos said new high-bandwidth memory supply would not arrive before late 2027, extending the shortage and keeping memory prices at record highs for now.\\n    Quote: “None of that supply, though, arrives before late 2027, which keeps the memory shortage going and record-high prices intact for now,” Partsinevelos said.\",\n   \"- e328 [fact; 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year; Data Center revenue was $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments were $119.0 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85.2% year over year, with Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and total supply-related commitments of $119.0 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e329 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Micron Technology ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] Micron said HBM4 was in high-volume shipments for its lead customer platform and HBM4E was in development, with volume production expected in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Micron’s HBM4, built on 1-beta DRAM, is in high-volume shipments for its lead customer platform, and HBM4E is in development, with volume production expected in calendar 2027.\",\n   \"- e330 [third_party_view; TIKR; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen estimates that NVIDIA earns a low-to-mid-teens share of its revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, TD Cowen estimates that Nvidia’s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range.\",\n   \"- e331 [third_party_view; TIKR; original source TD Cowen ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] TD Cowen reported that rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing.\\n    Quote: Rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing\",\n   \"- e332 [fact; TIKR; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported total quarterly revenue of $82 billion, up 85% year over year, and said it was the third consecutive quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Quote: The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e282; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e333 [fact; TIKR; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported quarterly Data Center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e334 [party_statement; TIKR; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA expects Vera CPU sales to reach $20 billion by the end of the current fiscal year.\\n    Quote: Nvidia also highlighted a new growth driver: its Vera CPU line, which the company expects to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of this fiscal year, a notable push into a market historically dominated by Intel and AMD.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e65; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e335 [third_party_view; es.tradingview.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:1bfc0e875ab1f26dcf48fb06 2026-07-11] Morgan Stanley said AI laboratories account for roughly 20% of NVIDIA’s demand, as enterprise AI adoption expands beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\\n    Quote: The bank noted that AI laboratories now account for roughly 20% of Nvidia’s demand, highlighting how enterprise AI adoption is expanding beyond hyperscale cloud providers.\",\n   \"- e170 [third_party_view; businesstimes.com.sg; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b 2026-07-06] A Bloomberg Intelligence survey expected Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips became harder to find and local firms took over, noting Beijing had urged Chinese technology firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use , become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e243, e386; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e240 [third_party_view; tradingview.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:a09988fd9c5c1a739a14f873 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence data cited by the outlet put NVIDIA's share of the server GPU market at 97% at end-2025, up from 95% at end-2024.\\n    Quote: the company holding 97% of the server GPU market at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024, according to Bloomberg Intelligence data cited in the source.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e304, e363; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e246 [fact; QZ; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ee0d6792b6bf98069cfe0cc6 2026-07-08] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia posted $81.6 billion in total revenue — an 85% increase from a year earlier\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e269, e368; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e312 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 revenue of $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Q2 FY27 guidance points to $91 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124, e319, e370; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e317 [fact; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 results put hard numbers behind the moat argument. The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156, e378; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e325 [third_party_view; Kristina Partsinevelos, as quoted by 24/7 Wall St.; original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:9ae96ca750b8e3962c47795f 2026-07-10] CNBC’s Kristina Partsinevelos said SK Hynix holds roughly 58% of the high-bandwidth memory market, while Micron and Samsung each hold roughly 21%, citing Counterpoint Research.\\n    Quote: “SK Hynix is the world leader in high bandwidth memory . The memory that feeds AI chips with roughly 58% of that market. Micron and Samsung competitors split roughly 21% each … as per Counterpoint Research.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e339 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated that NVIDIA held more than 90% of the AI training-chip market in 2025.\\n    Quote: According to Silicon Analysts , which compiles estimates from TrendForce, Morgan Stanley $MS , and TSMC $TSM capacity data, Nvidia 's share exceeded 90% in training in 2025.\",\n   \"- e340 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Silicon Analysts estimated NVIDIA's AI inference-chip market share at 60%–75% in 2025, amid competition from custom silicon.\\n    Quote: Its inference share sat between 60% and 75% over the same period, undercut by growing competition from custom silicon.\",\n   \"- e341 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source TechCrunch ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] TechCrunch reported that 1.4 million Amazon Trainium chips were deployed across three generations as of March, including more than one million Trainium2 chips running Anthropic's Claude.\\n    Quote: As of March, 1.4 million Trainium chips were deployed across three generations, according to TechCrunch , with Anthropic's Claude running on more than one million Trainium2 chips alone.\",\n   \"- e342 [fact; qz.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Amazon committed 2 GW of Trainium computing capacity to OpenAI.\\n    Quote: Amazon has also committed two gigawatts of Trainium computing capacity to OpenAI, putting its chips inside two of the industry's most prominent AI labs.\",\n   \"- e343 [fact; qz.com; original source AMD ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] AMD launched ROCm 7 and a free developer cloud.\\n    Quote: AMD launched ROCm 7 and a free developer cloud.\",\n   \"- e344 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated NVIDIA's overall AI-chip market share at 70%–95% depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the total market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\",\n   \"- e345 [fact; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] NVIDIA revenue increased 85% year over year in its past quarter; the item does not identify the quarter.\\n    Quote: During its past quarter, Nvidia's revenue increased at an 85% clip.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e104; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e346 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 96% during Q2; the item does not specify the fiscal year or comparison period.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect 96% growth during Q2.\",\n   \"- e348 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] Broadcom plans to ramp production of custom AI chips for Meta Platforms, Anthropic, and OpenAI starting late in 2026 and continuing into 2027.\\n    Quote: However, Broadcom is also making custom AI chips for Meta Platforms , Anthropic, and OpenAI, and production for those chips is scheduled to ramp up late this year and into next.\",\n   \"- e349 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author says the market expects NVIDIA to maintain its lead in growth for the full fiscal year, while Broadcom narrows the gap.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, the market still expects Nvidia to maintain its lead for the full fiscal year, though Broadcom is starting to close the gap.\",\n   \"- e350 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org; original source tech-insider.org 2026-07-12; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] NVIDIA had shipped no new gaming GPU architecture through September 2026, according to the outlet.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has shipped zero new gaming GPU architectures through September 2026 , breaking a release streak dating back roughly 30 years to the GeForce 256 in 1999.\",\n   \"- e351 [rumour; tech-insider.org, citing The Information; original source The Information ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reportedly shelved the RTX 50 Super refresh, including the completed-design 24GB RTX 5080 Super, in December 2025.\\n    Quote: The planned RTX 5080 Super (24GB) reached a completed-design stage before Nvidia shelved the entire RTX 50 Super refresh in December 2025 .\",\n   \"- e353 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source tech-insider.org 2026-07-12; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron reportedly sold out their 2026 HBM output to AI data-center customers.\\n    Quote: The cause is a global memory shortage: Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron have reportedly sold out their 2026 HBM output to AI data center customers.\",\n   \"- e354 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source Unnamed supply-chain sources, as reported by tech-insider.org ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reportedly pulled the RTX 5060 from retail and cut RTX 50-series production by an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026.\\n    Quote: The RTX 5060 has been pulled from retail, with RTX 50-series production cut an estimated 15% to 20% through at least Q3 2026.\",\n   \"- e355 [fact; tech-insider.org, reporting Jon Peddie Research figures; original source Jon Peddie Research ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Jon Peddie Research reported total discrete GPU shipments of 11.8 million units in Q1 2026, down 0.6% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: The most recent quarterly numbers from Jon Peddie Research show just how dominant Nvidia remains even as its gaming roadmap stalls. Total discrete GPU shipments came in at 11.8 million units for Q1 2026, down 0.6% from the prior quarter, a soft but not collapsing figure given rising component and memory costs.\",\n   \"- e356 [fact; tech-insider.org, reporting Tom’s Hardware; original source Tom’s Hardware ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Tom’s Hardware reported desktop GPU shipments of 12.5 million units by June 2026, a four-year high; Intel was the only vendor to gain share quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: By June 2026, shipments had swung the other way entirely: Tom’s Hardware reported desktop GPU shipments climbing to 12.5 million units , a four-year high, evidence that the production pullback has done little to cool actual demand even as prices keep climbing. Intel was the only vendor to gain share quarter-over-quarter, a small but symbolically important shift as Arc-series cards find a foothold \",\n   \"- e357 [fact; tech-insider.org, referring to the same report; original source The report’s publisher, not identified in this sentence ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] The report put the desktop GPU attach rate at 76%, up more than 33% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: One more data point from the same report stands out: the GPU attach rate per desktop PC shipped jumped to 76% , up more than 33% from the prior quarter.\",\n   \"- e358 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org, reporting Micron and Kearney’s PERLab; original source Micron and Kearney’s PERLab ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Micron suggested memory supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027 and may gradually return to balance by 2028; Kearney’s PERLab reportedly projected the shortage could last into 2030.\\n    Quote: Micron has since suggested supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027, with a gradual return to balance by 2028, while other forecasters take a bleaker view: an analysis from Kearney’s PERLab reportedly projects the shortage could persist into 2030 .\",\n   \"- e360 [fact; io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell plans to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026, a step in the development of an open-standard alternative for shared-memory workloads.\\n    Quote: Marvell expects to begin sampling its Structera S CXL 3.0 switch in calendar Q3 2026.\",\n   \"- e361 [party_statement; io-fund.com; original source Marvell ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] Marvell said its CXL business would exceed $1 billion in calendar 2028.\\n    Quote: Marvell says consumes CXL business to exceed $1 billion by calendar 2028\",\n   \"- e362 [third_party_view; io-fund.com; original source UBS ; from gnews:2dcfaef1a91c2976a4e347da 2026-07-12] UBS analysts estimated Marvell’s CXL revenue would reach $1 billion in calendar 2027 and $2 billion in calendar 2028.\\n    Quote: UBS seeing Marvell’s CXL revenue hitting $1 billion in calendar 2027 and doubling to $2 billion in calendar 2028.\",\n   \"- e363 [third_party_view; jpost.com; original source jpost.com 2026-07-12; from gnews:c14249088492921c802c839a 2026-07-12] NVIDIA’s server GPU market share was about 97% at the end of 2025, up from 95% at the end of 2024.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's firm grip on the server GPU market showed no signs of weakening, with its market share climbing to about 97% at the end of 2025, compared to 95% the previous year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e240; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e364 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said NVIDIA’s Vera CPU could expand its addressable market beyond GPUs and generate billions of dollars in additional revenue.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\",\n   \"- e365 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang introduced the Vera CPU, designed for AI workloads and agentic AI systems.\\n    Quote: During the company's latest product presentation, CEO Jensen Huang introduced the Vera CPU, a processor designed specifically for AI workloads and agentic AI systems.\",\n   \"- e366 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush said NVIDIA’s CPU move could significantly increase its total addressable market.\\n    Quote: Wedbush believes this move could significantly increase Nvidia's total addressable market.\",\n   \"- e367 [rumour; barchart.com; original source barchart.com ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Reports said NVIDIA has begun offering Vera processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\\n    Quote: Reports also suggest Nvidia has begun offering the new processors to cloud customers, including some in China where regulations allow.\",\n   \"- e368 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246, e387; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e369 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported first-quarter FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue climbed 92% YOY to $75.2 billion, highlighting that AI infrastructure remains the company's primary growth engine.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e199, e379; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e370 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided to approximately $91 billion of second-quarter FY2027 revenue, assuming no China Data Center sales.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e312, e388; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e371 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wall Street consensus ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wall Street consensus expected NVIDIA FY2027 revenue to exceed $300 billion and EPS to be $8.80 per share.\\n    Quote: Wall Street expects Nvidia to generate well over $300 billion in fiscal 2027 revenue, while consensus earnings estimates have moved to $8.80 per share.\",\n   \"- e372 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush said Vera gives NVIDIA an opportunity to expand its addressable market beyond GPUs and strengthen its position across AI infrastructure.\\n    Quote: Wedbush believes the Vera CPU platform gives Nvidia another opportunity to expand its TAM beyond GPUs, strengthening its competitive position across AI infrastructure.\",\n   \"- e373 [fact; fool.com (Adria Cimino); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported that quarterly revenue grew 198% to about $35 billion, a record.\\n    Quote: In the recent quarter, for example, the company reported revenue growth of 198% to about $35 billion dollars, a record level.\",\n   \"- e374 [fact; fool.com (Adria Cimino); original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported that quarterly net income rose 398% and operating margin was 72%.\\n    Quote: Net income soared 398%, and operating margin came in at 72%.\",\n   \"- e375 [third_party_view; fool.com (Adria Cimino); original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Counterpoint Research estimated that SK Hynix held 58% of the global HBM market at the end of the first quarter.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e325; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e376 [fact; fool.com (Adria Cimino); original source SK Hynix and NVIDIA ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix and NVIDIA signed a multi-year technology partnership for SK Hynix to supply memory across areas including AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\",\n   \"- e377 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by fool.com (Adria Cimino); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix had been NVIDIA's largest memory partner and would continue in that role.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\",\n   \"- e378 [fact; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its most recent fiscal quarter, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e317; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e379 [fact; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported data center revenue of $75.2 billion in its most recent fiscal quarter, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue of $75.2 billion climbed 92%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e369; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e380 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Broadcom reported AI chip revenue of $10.8 billion last quarter, up 143% year over year, and management forecast roughly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Quote: Its AI chip revenue jumped 143% year over year last quarter to $10.8 billion, and management sees roughly $16 billion this quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e201; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e381 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-08; from gnews:72628b3884888aef38bcb825 2026-07-12] NVIDIA announced on July 8 that its Nemotron 3 Ultra model was paired with LangChain's Deep Agents harness; the item reports no amount or period for the integration.\\n    Quote: On July 8, NVIDIA announced that its Nemotron 3 Ultra model achieved benchmark-leading performance when paired with LangChain's Deep Agents harness.\",\n   \"- e384 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source AMD ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] AMD recently acquired memory-optimization software platform Mext, which the author says positions AMD to offer a high-end server solution for inference.\\n    Quote: its recent acquisition of memory optimization software platform Mext\",\n   \"- e387 [fact; barchart.com (author), reporting NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e368; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e388 [party_statement; barchart.com (author), reporting NVIDIA management guidance; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided fiscal Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming no China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e370; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102, e246, e282, e394; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e103 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA projected fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% higher year over year.\\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124, e274, e404; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e121 [fact; 247wallst.com / Omor Ibne Ehsan; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue came in at $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e104, e156, e412; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e267 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source barchart.com 2026-07-09; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] The author said custom silicon could gradually erode NVIDIA's pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e395; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e269 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, for the quarter ended April 26, 2026.\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended April 26, Nvidia posted record revenue of $81.6 billion, an 85% year-over-year (YOY) increase\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246, e401; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e311 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year, and networking alone grew 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e199, e419; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e318 [fact; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA Data Center Networking revenue was $14.8 billion in Q1 FY2027, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Within that segment, Data Center Networking alone hit $14.8 billion, up 199% from a year earlier, reflecting surging demand for the Spectrum-X Ethernet and NVLink interconnect systems that travel with every rack-scale Blackwell deployment.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e272, e407, e415; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e319 [party_statement; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin of 75% and guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Quote: Non-GAAP gross margin came in at 75%, and management guided Q2 FY2027 revenue to $91 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e312, e417; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA management (outlook assumption); David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St. (upside interpretation) ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China; the author says a policy change permitting H200 exports could add upside.\\n    Quote: Notably, that outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China, meaning any policy thaw on H200 exports could represent additional upside.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e313, e410; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e333 [fact; TIKR; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c675b7c2548b02233ee7b05c 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported quarterly Data Center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e105, e403; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e370 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided to approximately $91 billion of second-quarter FY2027 revenue, assuming no China Data Center sales.\\n    Quote: Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e312, e388, e423; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e378 [fact; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:635f19578778394086009f6f 2026-07-12] Nvidia reported record total revenue of $81.6 billion in its most recent fiscal quarter, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: In its most recent fiscal quarter (ended in late April), revenue hit a record $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% from the prior quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e317, e402; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e387 [fact; barchart.com (author), reporting NVIDIA’s results; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA reported record FY2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: During the fiscal first quarter of 2027, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year-over-year (YOY).\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e368, e418; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e393 [party_statement; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to account for a larger share of future growth; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: It expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth as AI adoption expands.\",\n   \"- e394 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst David Jagielski; original source David Jagielski 2026-07-13; from gnews:9f0caa036b79269b16531bc3 2026-07-13] The author said NVIDIA was growing at 85% in its most recent quarter; the author did not identify the growth measure.\\n    Quote: Paying 32 times earnings for a business that's growing at a rate of 85% (in its most recent quarter) doesn't seem like a bad deal at all.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e395 [third_party_view; fool.com (Sean Williams); original source Sean Williams 2026-07-13; from gnews:e7e8cbf33738ceb5865837f0 2026-07-13] The author argues that GPU supply shortages support NVIDIA’s pricing power and gross margin, and that customer-developed chips occupying data-center capacity could erode that advantage.\\n    Quote: For starters, some of Nvidia's pricing power and otherworldly gross margin originates from persistent GPU supply shortages. If the company's top customers are developing chips that take up valuable data center real estate, Nvidia can quickly lose its biggest tailwind .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e267; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e396 [third_party_view; fool.com (Sean Williams); original source Sean Williams 2026-07-13; from gnews:e7e8cbf33738ceb5865837f0 2026-07-13] The author says hyperscalers’ internally developed AI chips are less costly and presumably more available than NVIDIA GPUs, whose demand has created a sizable backlog.\\n    Quote: Secondly, these internally developed chips are notably less costly than Nvidia's hardware and, presumably, more readily available (a function of demand creating a sizable backlog for Nvidia's GPUs).\",\n   \"- e397 [third_party_view; fool.com (Sean Williams); original source Sean Williams 2026-07-13; from gnews:e7e8cbf33738ceb5865837f0 2026-07-13] The author argues that cost-effective in-house AI chips at NVIDIA’s top customers may delay hyperscalers’ data-center upgrades and future NVIDIA GPU purchases.\\n    Quote: Lastly, AI chips developed by Nvidia's top customers may delay future upgrade cycles. Between Nvidia's accelerated innovation cycle, which is depreciating prior-generation GPUs, and the company's top customers developing cost-effective in-house solutions, hyperscalers may push out AI data center upgrades.\",\n   \"- e398 [rumour; gurufocus.com; original source The Information ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google reportedly approached neocloud companies about using its TPUs, a move that could increase competition with NVIDIA for AI-cloud demand.\\n    Quote: Google has approached so-called neocloud companies about using its tensor processing units, or TPUs, according to a report from The Information.\",\n   \"- e399 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source Nscale ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Nscale reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity, indicating continued demand for GPU-based cloud capacity relevant to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: One provider, Nscale, reportedly told Google that its active projects remain centered on GPU capacity.\",\n   \"- e401 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f4eb5206f2995f5dbb86c5e9 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.6 billion for its quarter ended April 26, 2026, up 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In its most recent quarter (ended April 26), it made $81.6 billion in revenue (up 85% year over year)\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e269; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e402 [fact; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter.\\n    Quote: For its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 26), Nvidia generated record revenue, up 85% year over year and 20% quarter over quarter to $81.6 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e378; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e403 [fact; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q1 data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: This drove adjusted earnings per share (EPS) that soared 140% to $1.87. The results were driven by record data center revenue of $75 billion, up 92%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e333; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e404 [party_statement; fool.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3a9054a950c410e249837c91 2026-07-13] NVIDIA management forecast FY2027 Q2 total revenue of $91 billion, up 95% year over year.\\n    Quote: Management expects its growth spurt to continue, forecasting year-over-year revenue growth of 95% to $91 billion in Q2.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e405 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e406 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion.\\n    Quote: with Data Center at $75.246 billion\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e407 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported that Data Center networking revenue grew 199% in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: networking alone up 199%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e318; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e408 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom reported Q2 FY2026 AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion, up 143% year over year, alongside total revenue of $22.187 billion, up 47.9%.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s Q2 FY2026 revenue hit $22.187 billion, up 47.9%, with AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion growing 143%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e201; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e409 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Hock Tan ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan said increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking was driving Broadcom’s sales mix.\\n    Quote: CEO Hock Tan said the mix is being “driven by increasing demand for custom AI accelerators and AI networking.”\",\n   \"- e410 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA’s Q2 guidance assumes zero Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue in Q2 guidance\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e320; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e411 [party_statement; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom management guided to $16.0 billion of AI revenue for Q3 FY2026, roughly 54% of total sales.\\n    Quote: management has already telegraphed $16.0 billion in AI revenue, roughly 54% of total sales.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e202; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e412 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.61 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Q1 FY27 revenue hit $81.61 billion, +85.2% YoY\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e121; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e413 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:301b0738dab6ca32e88b019a 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion.\\n    Quote: with Data Center at $75.25 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e122; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e414 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e415 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking alone did $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e318; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e416 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.2% year over year.\\n    Quote: Total revenue was $81.615 billion, growing 85.2%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e417 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 total revenue of $91 billion and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75%.\\n    Quote: But NVIDIA guided $91 billion for Q2 FY27 anyway, with a 75% non-GAAP gross margin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e319; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e418 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23%, for the quarter discussed.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA ( NASDAQ: NVDA ) followed with $81.615 billion and 85.23% growth.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e387; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e419 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92%, and Networking revenue growth of 199%, for the quarter discussed.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion, up 92%, with Networking exploding 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e311; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e420 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA shipped no H20 chips to China in the quarter discussed, compared with $4.6 billion in H20 sales to China a year earlier.\\n    Quote: Yet zero H20 chips shipped to China this quarter, versus $4.6 billion a year ago.\",\n   \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital expenditure plan to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute, a service to rent excess internal AI capacity to enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e233 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models on July 1, 2026.\",\n   \"- e422 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-13; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA has $119 billion in supply commitments, which the author says ties its business to hyperscaler order books.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA, by contrast, carries $119 billion in supply commitments, tying its fortunes to hyperscaler order books .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e129; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e423 [party_statement; 247wallst.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, excluding China, for the next quarter.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA guided to $91.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, explicitly excluding China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e370; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e424 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Dan Ives ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Dan Ives said demand for NVIDIA is outpacing supply by 12 to 1.\\n    Quote: Dan Ives Is Still Bullish on Nvidia: ‘We’re in the 3rd Inning of the AI Revolution,’ and Demand Is Outpacing Supply “12 to 1”\",\n   \"- e24 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027 and $554 billion in FY2028, versus trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e49, e226, e437, e438; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e33 [fact; Bram Berkowitz, The Motley Fool; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA reported FY2027 first-quarter revenue growth of 85% year over year.\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of Nvidia's fiscal year 2027, ending April 26, the company grew revenue 85% year over year, while diluted earnings per share soared by 140%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e102, e246, e282, e394, e475; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e274 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA guided to fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%, assuming no China Data Center compute revenue.\\n    Quote: Nvidia issued another optimistic outlook for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, forecasting revenue of $91 billion, plus or minus 2%, and a non-GAAP gross margin of about 75%. The guidance assumes no contribution from China Data Center compute revenue due to ongoing U.S. export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e103, e461; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e281 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34, e436; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e314 [fact; Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author cites NVIDIA revenue growth of 85.23% year over year and a 75.0% non-GAAP gross margin.\\n    Quote: For a business growing revenue 85.23% year over year at 75.0% non-GAAP gross margins, that is cheap on any historical comparison.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156, e462; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e317 [fact; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, and Data Center revenue of $75.2 billion.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 results put hard numbers behind the moat argument. The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e156, e378, e485; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e344 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Mizuho Securities and Silicon Analysts ; from gnews:2beadbce40c7f927f33d9fc5 2026-07-12] Mizuho Securities estimated NVIDIA's overall AI-chip market share at 70%–95% depending on segment; Silicon Analysts projected it would settle near 75% as the total market grows beyond $200 billion.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's overall AI chip market share, estimated by Mizuho Securities at between 70% and 95% depending on segment, is projected by Silicon Analysts to settle near 75% as the total market expands past $200 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e444; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e388 [party_statement; barchart.com (author), reporting NVIDIA management guidance; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA management guided fiscal Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, assuming no China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, management guided Q2 revenue to approximately $91 billion, despite assuming zero China data-center revenue because of export restrictions.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e370, e483; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e394 [third_party_view; fool.com analyst David Jagielski; original source David Jagielski 2026-07-13; from gnews:9f0caa036b79269b16531bc3 2026-07-13] The author said NVIDIA was growing at 85% in its most recent quarter; the author did not identify the growth measure.\\n    Quote: Paying 32 times earnings for a business that's growing at a rate of 85% (in its most recent quarter) doesn't seem like a bad deal at all.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e33, e484; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e405 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 total revenue of $81.615 billion, up 85.23% year over year.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s Q1 FY2027 revenue reached $81.615 billion, up 85.23%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e246, e458; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e407 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported that Data Center networking revenue grew 199% in Q1 FY2027.\\n    Quote: networking alone up 199%\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e318, e471; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e408 [fact; 247Wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Broadcom ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] Broadcom reported Q2 FY2026 AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion, up 143% year over year, alongside total revenue of $22.187 billion, up 47.9%.\\n    Quote: Broadcom’s Q2 FY2026 revenue hit $22.187 billion, up 47.9%, with AI semiconductor sales of $10.80 billion growing 143%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e201, e456; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e414 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.246 billion, up 92% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue hit $75.246 billion , up 92% YoY.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e199, e478; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e415 [fact; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA reported Q1 FY2027 Data Center networking revenue of $14.8 billion, up 199% year over year.\\n    Quote: Data Center networking alone did $14.8 billion, up 199%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e318, e459; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e417 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA guided to Q2 FY2027 total revenue of $91 billion and a non-GAAP gross margin of 75%.\\n    Quote: But NVIDIA guided $91 billion for Q2 FY27 anyway, with a 75% non-GAAP gross margin.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e319, e474; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital expenditure plan to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute, a service to rent excess internal AI capacity to enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e460; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e233 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models on July 1, 2026.\",\n   \"- e422 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-13; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e51