{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,re; x=json.load(open(\\\"controls/control-packet-5.json\\\"))[0]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(e for e in x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"] if re.search(r\\\"91 billion|91B|75%|accelerating growth|100 b|first shipments|first ship|ramp|volume shipments|±2|plus or minus\\\",e,re.I)))'\"","aggregated_output":"- e101 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA Data Center revenue grew 92% year over year and 21% sequentially in fiscal Q1 2027.\n    Quote: Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.\n- e103 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA projected fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% higher year over year.\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e103 [party_statement; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA projected fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of approximately $91 billion, nearly 95% higher year over year.\n    Quote: For the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA projects revenues of approximately $91 billion, representing nearly 95% year-over-year growth.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e124, e274; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e270 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-05-20; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter non-GAAP E